CLASS:PUBLIC
DESCRIPTION:After reading the learning materials provided\, go through the 
 following scenario and respond to the follow- up questions before the set 
 deadline. \n\nScenario\n\nThe African Leadership University is considerin
 g replacing the online classes with in-person classes to improve student e
 ngagement and academic integrity. Students and members of faculty who supp
 ort the idea argue that the face to face (in-person) learning strengthens 
 interaction\, discipline\, and critical discussion. On the other hand\, ot
 hers raise concerns about reduced access\, loss of flexibility\, and highe
 r costs for students who work or commute.\n\n* As a critical thinker\, how
  would you gather information from students\, faculty\, and institutional 
 data to analyze these competing claims?\n\n* Explain how critical thinking
  skills would help you extract evidence from the collected information and
  make a decision.\n\n(Note: Reply to at least two people)
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Week 1: Discussion Board- Introduction to Critical Thinking [Critic
 al_Thinking]
URL;VALUE=URI:https://alueducation.instructure.com/calendar?include_context
 s=course_3097&month=09&year=2026#assignment_43978
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>After reading the learning materials provid
 ed\, go through the following scenario and respond to the follow- up quest
 ions before the set deadline.&nbsp\;</p>\n<p data-pm-slice="0 0 []"><stron
 g>Scenario</strong></p>\n<p data-pm-slice="0 0 []">The African Leadership 
 University is considering replacing the online classes with in-person clas
 ses to improve student engagement and academic integrity. Students and mem
 bers of faculty who support the idea argue that the face to face (in-perso
 n) learning strengthens interaction\, discipline\, and critical discussion
 . On the other hand\, others raise concerns about reduced access\, loss of
  flexibility\, and higher costs for students who work or commute.</p>\n<ul
 >\n<li>As a critical thinker\, how would you gather information from stude
 nts\, faculty\, and institutional data to analyze these competing claims?<
 /li>\n<li>Explain how critical thinking skills would help you extract evid
 ence from the collected information and make a decision.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><
 em><strong>(Note: Reply to at least two people)</strong></em></p>
END:VEVENT
