CLASS:PUBLIC
DESCRIPTION:**Disclaimer: While this pre-course reflection is graded as com
 plete or incomplete\, it will prove essential for responding to the end-of
 -course final assessment. \n\n-------------------------------------------
 ------------------------------------\nCourse Prerequisite Assignment: Pers
 onal Reflection on Policy in Your Community\n-----------------------------
 --------------------------------------------------\n\nPurpose:\n--------\n
 \nThis essay serves as the starting point of your learning journey in this
  course. The goal is not to test your knowledge\, but to encourage you to 
 reflect on your personal experiences with policies in your community. By w
 riting this essay\, you will begin to develop your own perspective on poli
 cymaking\, which we will revisit and deepen as the course progresses.\n\nI
 nstructions:\n-------------\n\nWrite a reflective essay (300–500 words) 
 on your personal experiences and thoughts about policies in your community
 . Your essay should address the following guiding questions:\n\nWhat is on
 e policy that you have observed in your community\, school\, or country?\n
 \nHow has this policy affected you\, your family\, or your community?\n\nD
 o you think this policy has achieved what it was intended to do? Why or wh
 y not?\n\nWhat challenges or opportunities do you see in the way policies 
 are made or implemented in your community?\n\nWhat does “policy” mean 
 to you personally?\n\nImportant Notes:\n----------------\n\nThere are no r
 ight or wrong answers. We are more interested in your individual perspecti
 ve and experiences.\n\nUse clear and simple language. This is not a resear
 ch paper\; it is a reflection.\n\nBe as specific as you can. Give examples
  from your personal life or observations.\n\nHow this assignment will be u
 sed:\n---------------------------------\n\nThis essay will not be graded f
 or correctness\, but for completion and effort. It will serve as a baselin
 e to help you and your instructors see how your understanding of policies 
 develops throughout the course. At the end of the course\, you will reflec
 t again on your views and compare them with those in your first essay.\n\n
 You can supplement your written essay with any form of media that will hel
 p support your reflection\, e.g.\, photographs\, diagrams\, data tables\, 
 data visualizations\, external links to audio/video content\, etc. Please
  upload your response as a Word document or a PDF file that includes bot
 h your written response and the relevant media. Links to Google documents
  and folders will not be accepted.\n\nRequired Formatting\n--------------
 -----\n\n* Font:  Times New Roman\n\n* Font Size: 12\n\n* Font Color: Bla
 ck \n\n* Line Spacing: 1 \n\n* Align: Justify text \n\n* 300-500 words\
 n\n* This assignment does not need a reference list\, as it is your own th
 oughts.
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Pre-Course Reflection:Personal Reflection on Policy in Your Communi
 ty [Structured_Controversy]
