CLASS:PUBLIC
DESCRIPTION:Formative Assessment 1: Systems Thinking and Problem Diagnosis\
 n\nOverview\n\nThis formative 1 assessment covers weeks 1-4 and is designe
 d to help you deeply understand\, research\, and map a complex\, mission-b
 ased problem within your area. You will define the problem\, back it up wi
 th credible research\, identify the key stakeholders\, and map the systemi
 c variables at play.\n\nThis assessment is divided into four interconnecte
 d parts. Please read the instructions for each part carefully before submi
 tting.\n\n \n\nPart 1: Problem Statement\n\nObjective\n\nClearly define a
  single\, focused problem that relates to your mission/Grand Challenges an
 d Global Opportunities (GCGO) interests.\n\nInstructions\n\nYour problem s
 tatement must be rooted in a community you can easily access for the durat
 ion of the course. This is crucial because subsequent assessments will req
 uire you to speak to stakeholders\, conduct interviews\, and explore the s
 ystem in detail.\n\nApply the 5 Ws: Start by answering Who\, What\, Where\
 , When\, and Why.\n\nKeep it Concise: Your final problem statement should 
 be only 1 to 2 sentences long (maximum 30–50 words).\n\nFocus: Address o
 nly one core problem.\n\nNo Solutions: Do not suggest or imply a solution 
 yet\; focus entirely on diagnosing the current issue.\n\nSupport: Include 
 relevant citations where necessary to ground the problem in reality.\n\n 
 \n\nPart 2: System Mapping Part 1 (Causal Loop Diagram Draft)\n\nObjective
 \n\nVisualize the systemic nature of your problem by mapping the cause-and
 -effect relationships between variables.\n\nInstructions\n\nSubmit the fir
 st draft of your Causal Loop Diagram (CLD). This initial version does not 
 have to be flawless\, but it must clearly show the elements\, variables\, 
 and links that relate to your problem and form the foundation of a system.
  You will continue to refine this map throughout the course as you conduct
  deeper research.\n\nTools: You can use Kumu\, Jamboard\, Google Slides\, 
 or any digital mapping tool of your choice.\n\nPriority: The clarity and l
 ogical content of the loops/relationships are the main priorities for this
  submission.\n\n \n\nPart 3: Research Foundation (Annotated Bibliography)
 \n\nObjective\n\nGather\, organize\, and evaluate the evidence and data su
 rrounding your chosen problem statement. An annotated bibliography helps y
 ou track your sources and allows your facilitator to evaluate the relevanc
 e and credibility of your research.\n\nInstructions\n\nConduct preliminary
  research on your problem and provide an annotated bibliography that inclu
 des:\n\n*\n\nFive (5) Secondary Sources: For each source\, provide the ful
 l citation and a brief paragraph explaining how it contributes to your und
 erstanding of the problem and why it is useful to your research.\n\n*\n\nO
 ne (1) Primary Source: Identify at least one primary source e.g.\,intervie
 w\, that you will use\, and justify its direct relevance to your target co
 mmunity or problem.\n\nFormatting: Ensure all citations strictly follow AP
 A 7th edition style.\n\n \n\nPart 4: Stakeholder Analysis & Mapping\n\nOb
 jective\n\nIdentify and analyze the human actors and organizations within 
 your system\, examining how much influence and interest they have regardin
 g your defined problem.\n\nInstructions\n\nIdentify at least 10 stakeholde
 rs relevant to your problem's system. For example\, in a school system\, s
 tudents may have high interest but low power\, whereas the school board ho
 lds high influence/power over final approvals.\n\nYour submission must inc
 lude:\n\n*\n\nAn Influence/Interest Grid mapping all 10+ stakeholders into
  their respective quadrants (High/Low Power\, High/Low Interest). You may 
 use this template: [[Influence/Interest Grid Template]] (https://docs.goog
 le.com/presentation/d/1V37gB8UuNPbowm646xZvHAiKOm5YuJ4Pom7L0R5Pr-Y/edit?us
 p=sharing) (Be sure to make a copy!).\n\n*\n\nA brief analysis highlightin
 g relationships between stakeholders\, noting potential points of conflict
  or strategic alignment.\n\nSubmission Guidelines\n\nTo maintain a clean w
 orkflow\, please compile and submit your work according to the following f
 ormat rules:\n\nFile Types: Parts 1\, 3\, and 4 must be compiled into a si
 ngle PDF\, Word Document\, or PowerPoint presentation.\n\nCausal Loop Diag
 ram (Part 2): You must submit a direct\, accessible link to your live Kumu
  or Jamboard map within your document. If you used a slide-based tool\, en
 sure Part 2 is saved directly into your main PDF/Word submission. No other
  miscellaneous file types will be accepted.\n\nN.B. Start working on this 
 assessment earlier as there are no extensions for an assessment that has b
 een available for 4 weeks. 
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Formative Assessment 1 ( Week 1-4 ): Systems Thinking and Problem D
 iagnosis [Systems_Thinking_and_Gap_Analysis]
