 1) Primary Source:</strong><span> Identify at least one primary source e.g
 .\,interview\, that you will use\, and justify its direct relevance to you
 r target community or problem.</span></p>\n</li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong>Format
 ting:</strong><span> Ensure all citations strictly follow </span><strong>A
 PA 7th edition</strong><span> style.</span></p>\n<p><span>&nbsp\;</span></
 p>\n<p><span style="color: #e62429\;"><strong>Part 4: Stakeholder Analysis
  &amp\; Mapping</strong></span></p>\n<p><strong>Objective</strong></p>\n<p
 ><span>Identify and analyze the human actors and organizations within your
  system\, examining how much influence and interest they have regarding yo
 ur defined problem.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Instructions</strong></p>\n<p><
 span>Identify </span><strong>at least 10 stakeholders</strong><span> relev
 ant to your problem's system. For example\, in a school system\, students 
 may have high </span><i><span>interest</span></i><span> but low </span><i>
 <span>power</span></i><span>\, whereas the school board holds high </span>
 <i><span>influence/power</span></i><span> over final approvals.</span></p>
 \n<p><span>Your submission must include:</span></p>\n<ol>\n<li>\n<p><span>
  An </span><strong>Influence/Interest Grid</strong><span> mapping all 10+ 
 stakeholders into their respective quadrants (High/Low Power\, High/Low In
 terest). You may use this template: </span><a class="inline_disabled" href
 ="https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1V37gB8UuNPbowm646xZvHAiKOm5YuJ4P
 om7L0R5Pr-Y/edit?usp=sharing" target="_blank"><strong>[Influence/Interest 
 Grid Template]</strong></a> <i><span>(Be sure to make a copy!)</span></i><
 span>.</span></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span> A brief analysis highlighting </
 span><strong>relationships</strong><span> between stakeholders\, noting po
 tential points of conflict or strategic alignment.</span></p>\n</li>\n</ol
 >\n<p><span style="color: #e62429\;"><strong>Submission Guidelines</strong
 ></span></p>\n<p><span>To maintain a clean workflow\, please compile and s
 ubmit your work according to the following format rules:</span></p>\n<p><s
 trong>File Types:</strong><span> Parts 1\, 3\, and 4 must be compiled into
  a single </span><strong>PDF\, Word Document\, or PowerPoint presentation<
 /strong><span>.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Causal Loop Diagram (Part 2):</stro
 ng><span> You must submit a direct\, accessible link to your live </span><
 strong>Kumu</strong><span> or </span><strong>Jamboard</strong><span> map w
 ithin your document. If you used a slide-based tool\, ensure Part 2 is sav
 ed directly into your main PDF/Word submission. No other miscellaneous fil
 e types will be accepted.</span></p>\n<p><strong>N.B. <span style="color: 
 #e62429\;">Start working on this assessment earlier as there are no extens
 ions for an assessment that has been available for 4 weeks.&nbsp\;</span><
 /strong></p>\n<p><br><br></p>
END:VEVENT
