 p data-start="78" data-end="468">This assignment asks you to reflect on ho
 w your thinking about unemployment in Tarifa evolved throughout the cycle.
  You will revisit your initial position\, examine how it was formed\, and 
 present your final\, evidence-based stance after engaging with classmates 
 and course materials. The goal is to demonstrate both intellectual growth 
 and strong argumentation grounded in your assigned role.</p>\n<h3 data-sec
 tion-id="1vpev9s" data-start="470" data-end="519"><span role="text"><stron
 g data-start="474" data-end="517">Assignment Instructions (600–700 words
 )</strong></span></h3>\n<p data-start="520" data-end="594">Write a structu
 red essay that integrates your initial and final positions.</p>\n<p data-s
 tart="596" data-end="1086">Begin by explaining your original stance on how
  employment can become a reality for the people of Tarifa before the class
  discussions. Use concrete examples\, evidence\, or reasoning that shaped 
 your thinking\, such as prior knowledge\, assumptions\, global examples\, 
 or initial readings. Your explanation should also reflect how your perspec
 tive aligned with your assigned role\, informed by your understanding of t
 hat figure’s background and priorities.</p>\n<p data-start="1088" data-e
 nd="1365">Next\, discuss how your thinking evolved throughout the structur
 ed controversy and class discussions. Identify specific ideas\, arguments\
 , or interactions that challenged\, strengthened\, or refined your positio
 n. Explain whether your views shifted or became more nuanced\, and why.</p
 >\n<p data-start="1367" data-end="2017">Then\, present your final position
  on the question: <em data-start="1418" data-end="1481">How can employment
  become a reality for the people of Tarifa?</em> Clearly indicate which of
  the two approaches discussed in class you chose and justify your decision
  using strong evidence and reasoning. Your argument should reflect an unde
 rstanding of the Tarifa context\, remain consistent with your assigned rol
 e\, and consider efficiency\, equity\, empowerment\, and sustainability. S
 upport your position using at least two forms of evidence\, such as facts\
 , expert opinions\, real-world examples\, statistics\, or logical reasonin
 g. You are encouraged to draw on global examples where relevant.</p>\n<p d
 ata-start="2019" data-end="2265">Finally\, identify one real employment-re
 lated policy (2016–2026) from your country and briefly explain how it co
 uld have informed your group’s consensus-building process. Discuss its s
 trengths and limitations\, and connect them to your final position.</p>\n<
